  "id": "COMPOUND:30035 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Erysimoside is implicated in the interaction with A549 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link being its targeting of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, which in turn has A549 as its target. This suggests a cascade of molecular interactions where Erysimoside acts as a modulator of a metabolic pathway, influencing A549 cell behavior. Complementary evidence from other paths shows that Erysimoside can also target Ataxin-2, which is further targeted by a complex compound, both of which ultimately lead to A549. These findings highlight the potential of Erysimoside to modulate cellular processes in A549 cells, possibly through the regulation of metabolic enzymes or other molecular targets. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Erysimoside in influencing A549 cell function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
